' Same-block funding decision for offered-funded deploys (DR-65, decision D2).
' Deploys that compete for one physical purse form one funding decision, as P1's
' "simultaneous arrival" paragraph requires: if their combined holds exceed the
' purse supply at the original root R0, every member of the group is rejected.
' Accepted members execute in canonical order; the held-capacity guard keeps the
' holds of later members available.
'
' Changed by DR-134 (implementation note 3 of DR-65): the decision pass checks
' every member at R0 before any runtime entry; members that draw one grant also
' form one group; each member caps its settlement capacity by the later holds
' at R_{i-1} (option B, design section 8.4); dev's play budget applies between
' members, and the truncation rule re-runs the shipped prefix when needed.
'
' Source of truth: docs/casper/theory/cost-accounting-decision-records.md (DR-65);
'                  publications/cost-accounting/cost-accounted-rho.tex (sec:deploy-boundaries).
' Palette:  candidates = supply blue · DR-64 check = gate teal · grouping = process lilac
'           execution = pool green · capacity cap = capability indigo
'           settlement = note green · user failure = note amber
'           play budget and re-run = delta orange · reject = red · decisions = control amber
' Render:  plantuml -tsvg docs/casper/theory/diagrams/offered-same-block-funding-groups.puml
'          (or: ./render.sh offered-same-block-funding-groups.puml)

@startuml offered-same-block-funding-groups
!include palette.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $ca_neutral
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #333333
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor $ca_control
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #333333
skinparam PartitionBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
title Same-block funding groups, the capacity cap and the held-capacity guard (DR-65)

start
partition "Decision pass at <latex>R_0</latex>, before any runtime entry (proposer and every validator)" {
  :pending offered candidates in canonical order\n(valid-after block, timestamp, identity)\nplay sorts the batch · replay rejects any other order\nor a repeated member; <<$ca_supply>>
  :DR-64 check of each candidate\non its own signed sources at <latex>R_0</latex>; <<$ca_gate>>
  if (a candidate fails alone?) then (yes)
    :the first such candidate is rejected alone\n(it cannot sink other candidates)\nplay: quarantine it, retry the rest from <latex>R_0</latex>\nreplay: reject the block; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
    detach
  else (no)
  endif
  :union-find over custodies and grant identifiers\nmembers that share a purse or a grant form one group <latex>G</latex>; <<$ca_process>>
  if (<latex>\exists p:\ \sum_{m \in G} \mathrm{hold}_m(p) > \mathrm{supply}_{R_0}(p)</latex>\nor the draws on one grant exceed its remaining ceiling?) then (yes)
    :reject every member of <latex>G</latex>\nno effect · no charge\nplay: quarantine <latex>G</latex>, retry the rest from <latex>R_0</latex>; <<$ca_rejectfill>>
    note right $ca_note_red
      P1 simultaneous arrival:
      not enough resources for all
      members, so none of them begins.
    end note
    detach
  else (no · every group accepted)
  endif
  :later holds of each accepted member <latex>i</latex>\n<latex>L_i(p) = \sum_{j > i} \mathrm{hold}_j(p)</latex>; <<$ca_process>>
}
partition "Execution of the accepted members, in canonical order" {
  repeat
    :member <latex>i</latex> funds from <latex>R_0</latex>\nand executes from <latex>R_{i-1}</latex>\nin a fresh offered runtime; <<$ca_pool>>
    :settlement inputs read at <latex>R_{i-1}</latex>\n<latex>\mathrm{cap}_i(p) = \min\bigl(\mathrm{caps}_i(p),\ \mathrm{balance}_{R_{i-1}}(p) - L_i(p)\bigr)</latex>; <<$ca_capability>>
    if (<latex>\mathrm{balance}_{\mathrm{after}}(p) - \mathrm{debit}_i(p) \geq L_i(p)</latex>\nfor every debited or later-held purse?) then (holds)
      :settle member <latex>i</latex>\ncharge the measured use\n(the unused hold never leaves the purse); <<$ca_note_green>>
    else (guard fails)
      :member <latex>i</latex> is a charged user failure\nroll back to <latex>R_{i-1}</latex> · pay billable work and fee\nfrom the restored balance, under the same cap; <<$ca_note_amber>>
    endif
  repeat while (more accepted members, and dev's play budget not spent?) is (yes)
  ->no;
  if (the budget stopped the batch, and a group spans the cut\nor a shipped member settled as a guard rollback?) then (yes)
    :play the shipped prefix again from <latex>R_0</latex>\nwith no budget, at most once; <<$ca_delta>>
  else (no)
    :ship the members as played; <<$ca_delta>>
  endif
  :system deploys run from <latex>R_n</latex> · publish the block; <<$ca_note_green>>
  :validators recompute the order, the groups, the later holds,\nthe caps and the guards over the shipped members\n(they re-guard a committed success that has later holds); <<$ca_note_green>>
}
stop

legend bottom
  |= colour |= meaning |
  |<$ca_supply>| pending candidates |
  |<$ca_gate>| DR-64 individual funding check |
  |<$ca_process>| grouping and later holds |
  |<$ca_pool>| execution with committed holds |
  |<$ca_capability>| capacity cap by the later holds |
  |<$ca_note_green>| settlement and publication |
  |<$ca_note_amber>| charged user failure (held-capacity guard) |
  |<$ca_delta>| dev's play budget and the truncation rule |
  |<$ca_rejectfill>| rejection with no effect |
  |<$ca_control>| decision |
endlegend

@enduml
